                                                "sense_id": "58fc63e1-6032-3815-ab60-7cd1dcbea66d",
                                                "text": "A tray filled with pawns, prepared with the usual ingredients, as lime cuttie (a bitter gum), betel-nut, tobacco, spices, &c."
                                            },
                                            {
                                                "example_id": "792ae016-bc6f-432a-9924-d93eb12fbe05",
                                                "sense_id": "58fc63e1-6032-3815-ab60-7cd1dcbea66d",
                                                "text": "To our English taste, pawn is very offensive; but the natives of India relish it, and regard it as a necessity. It is much eaten by Mohammedans of both sexes, and by the natives of Bengal."
                                            }
                                        ]
                                    }
                                ]
                            },
